          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On February 25, 2015, at 6:10 PM, a witness is driving when they spot a high in the sky, colored phenomenon heading northwest. A plane passes nearby. The sky is very clear. A yellow or red oval, very bright, observed for 5 minutes at sunset, appears as a small cloud retro-lit by the setting sun. This could be water vapor from an airplane trail, or a cloud. Airplane trails are described as a fuse or a V. In this case, the presence of a cloud is more likely. Its disappearance in one or two minutes is not very surprising. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a small cloud at sunset.",
